sections.text:
Quick rotations with great damage output. Pretty refreshing compared to the wave of Hybrids with longer rotations that recently released. Great damage output also makes her completely viable to use as a strong Main DPS, particularly in AoE scenarios like Whimpering Wastes;

 Fits in several teams thanks to being able to apply both Spectro Frazzle and Aero Erosion as well as buff Aero DMG via Solo Concert/Gusts of Welkin/Signature weapon;

 Damage over time actually contributes a good amount of off-field damage for once, including her small waves of damage when singing;

 Aero Erosion and Spectro Frazzle from Ultimate apply repeatedly off-field, even across multiple waves of enemies;

 Rotations don’t suffer much from being interrupted by enemies as dodges don’t reset Basic Attack chains;

 High potential for cancelling & improving her rotation (not too difficult to do either) — good baseline, great ceiling;

 Sequence value is low, meaning S0 allows her to already get close to full potential (can be a con if you’re interested in Sequences though).

May need you to build 2 separate Echo Sets for her to access her team flexibility (Gusts of Welkin is only used in Aero teams, Moonlit Clouds for general use);

 A lot of her potential is locked behind her Signature weapon in Aero teams or as a Main DPS;

 Sings during her Ultimate which replaces a potentially epic battle theme by a silly song.
